  "body": "Found while working #1050 (held work on `mkinney:issue/1050-developed-band-exit`, commit 16e129bb, stacked on #1138).\n\n**What happens.** With #1050's held change (the growth rings' disc phase also held on a coarser rim, so the plan out of the bore takes smaller steps), `adaptive_hsm::hsm_report_full_resolution` (release, `--ignored`) turns red on the **narrow slot 14x60**: the verifier names one `RapidInStock` (move 14108) and the reader counts 4 descents into stock for 2 levels (law: 2). Every other fixture and every other heavy lane run stays green (motion lib `--include-ignored adaptive`: 32/32, both #1051 budget twins included).\n\n**Where.** A ladder retract hop (`lift::schedule`, `lift_link::landing`) lands at (17.407, 8.956), 0.3 above the floor, then ramps down its lead. The posted program has not cut a strip along the slot's wall there yet: the footprint point (17.407, 13.946) is 5.065 mm from every earlier cutting move on that level (tool r = 5, wall at y = 14) - a ~0.05 mm strip inside the wall margin that only the last lap takes. The planner's lift stock (`out.ras`) reads the landing as clear (`stock_clear(rim + h)` passed), so the posted program and the stock the hop law reads disagree by less than a planner cell (D/120 = 0.083 mm). Adding a wall-clearance test to `landing` (footprint off the wall cells too) changes nothing: the landing is not the fallback, the strip is simply not on the planner's grid.\n\n**Why it matters.** The verifier blocks the post (not silent), but any lifted plan whose hop lands next to a wall margin can hit it; on main the narrow slot's hops land elsewhere by chance.\n\nDone means: a hop never lands where the posted program leaves stock under the footprint (the planner's hop law reads the stock the posted moves leave, or keeps a margin that covers the sub-cell strip), pinned on the narrow slot with #1050's change applied, and `hsm_report_full_resolution` green.\n",
